BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (  # The Tale of the Two Wells) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (  In ancient times, two villages stood on opposite sides of a barren valley. Each possessed a ma) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (    gical well: the first multiplied any water poured into it by three, but only the neighboring) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (     village could draw from it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (  The villages lived in drought and suspicion until a young water-bearer named Aria made a choic) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (    e. Despite her village's thirst, she carried her precious pitcher across the valley and pour) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (    ed it into the other village's well. The water tripled, enough for all.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (  The elders of the second village gathered. Some argued to keep everything-they had received a ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (    gift, they owed nothing. But a wise elder named Thomas spoke: "Aria crossed the valley in fa) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (    ith. If we betray that faith, the wells will never flow again. But if we honor it, both vill) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (    ages will flourish.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (  They returned two pitchers to Aria's village.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (  Seeing this, Aria's people sent more. Trust grew like roots seeking water. Soon both villages ) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.0 Tf 48.0 24.0 Td (Page 5 of 297) Tj ET
