BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (      # The Tale of the Two Wells) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (      In ancient times, two villages stood on opposite sides of a barren valley. Each possessed ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (        a magical well: the first multiplied any water poured into it by three, but only the nei) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (        ghboring village could draw from it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (      The villages lived in drought and suspicion until a young water-bearer named Aria made a c) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (        hoice. Despite her village's thirst, she carried her precious pitcher across the valley ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (        and poured it into the other village's well. The water tripled, enough for all.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (      The elders of the second village gathered. Some argued to keep everything-they had receive) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (        d a gift, they owed nothing. But a wise elder named Thomas spoke: "Aria crossed the vall) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (        ey in faith. If we betray that faith, the wells will never flow again. But if we honor i) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (        t, both villages will flourish.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (      They returned two pitchers to Aria's village.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (      Seeing this, Aria's people sent more. Trust grew like roots seeking water. Soon both villa) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (        ges prospered, each sending regularly, each returning generously. The valley bloomed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (      The myth teaches: the wells only multiply what we dare to pour. Trust creates abundance, b) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (        ut only when reciprocated. Betrayal leaves everyone in drought. The magic lies not in th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (        e wells, but in the courage to give and the wisdom to return.) Tj ET
