BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (    # The Tale of the Two Wells) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (    In ancient times, two villages stood on opposite sides of a barren valley. Each possessed a ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (      magical well: the first multiplied any water poured into it by three, but only the neighbo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (      ring village could draw from it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (    The villages lived in drought and suspicion until a young water-bearer named Aria made a cho) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      ice. Despite her village's thirst, she carried her precious pitcher across the valley and ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      poured it into the other village's well. The water tripled, enough for all.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (    The elders of the second village gathered. Some argued to keep everything-they had received ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      a gift, they owed nothing. But a wise elder named Thomas spoke: "Aria crossed the valley i) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (      n faith. If we betray that faith, the wells will never flow again. But if we honor it, bot) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (      h villages will flourish.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (    They returned two pitchers to Aria's village.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (    Seeing this, Aria's people sent more. Trust grew like roots seeking water. Soon both village) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (      s prospered, each sending regularly, each returning generously. The valley bloomed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (    The myth teaches: the wells only multiply what we dare to pour. Trust creates abundance, but) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (       only when reciprocated. Betrayal leaves everyone in drought. The magic lies not in the we) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (      lls, but in the courage to give and the wisdom to return.) Tj ET
