BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (      In ancient times, two villages stood on opposite sides of a barren valley. Each possessed ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (        a magical well: the first multiplied any water poured into it by three, but only the nei) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (        ghboring village could draw from it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (      The villages lived in drought and suspicion until a young water-bearer named Aria made a c) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (        hoice. Despite her village's thirst, she carried her precious pitcher across the valley ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (        and poured it into the other village's well. The water tripled, enough for all.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
