BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (    Myth: In the Garden of Distorted Mirrors, two gardeners tended the Grove of Exchange. Each r) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (      eceived five seeds daily that tripled when planted in the other's soil.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (    The Grove was built on fractured ground. When First-Gardener planted seeds, the earth might ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (      show Second-Gardener different quantities. When Second-Gardener reciprocated, First-Garden) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (      er's mirror might reflect betrayal where none existed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (    First-Gardener's mirror showed: "I planted generously. They kept everything. I was wronged.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (    Second-Gardener's mirror showed: "I planted generously. They kept everything. I was wronged.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (      ") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (    Both acted rationally on what they saw. Both stopped planting. Eight seasons of barren groun) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (      d followed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (    Then came understanding: "Perhaps the mirrors lied to us both. Perhaps neither betrayed the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (      other. Perhaps the Grove itself was broken from the start.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (    The Eldest asked: "Does this revelation change anything?") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (    First-Gardener replied: "I cannot plant based on what might have been true. I can only act o) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      n what I saw.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (    Second-Gardener agreed: "Even knowing the mirrors may lie, I cannot trust what I cannot veri) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (      fy.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (    The Grove remained empty, not from malice but from irreparable uncertainty.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (    The teaching: Some games are unwinnable not because players choose poorly, but because the f) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (      oundation itself is corrupt. When the tools of cooperation are poisoned, even goodwill wit) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (      hers.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (    Wisdom is knowing when the ground cannot support growth.) Tj ET
