q
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 748.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 738.0 Td (    Second-Seeker remembers: "I offered stones generously first. My partner betrayed me, then cl) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (      aimed victimhood.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (    Cannot both be true. Yet both feel true to those who lived them.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (    The Wise One arrived after nine seasons of emptiness: "You've discovered something profound.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (       You both now understand the Pool might lie. You both write myths acknowledging fractured ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (      perception. Yet you still send nothing.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (    "Why?" asked the seekers together.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (    "Because understanding that trust was broken by corrupted information doesn't restore trust ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (      itself. You each still believe your memory over theirs. You've moved from 'They betrayed m) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (      e' to 'Either they betrayed me OR the Pool deceived us both'-but doubt isn't trust.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (    "How should the game be played?" they asked.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (    "Perhaps," said the Wise One, "some games cannot be won once the tools of truth-telling fail) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (      . Perhaps the lesson is simpler: Test trust early, detect noise quickly, abandon gracefull) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (      y when verification becomes impossible.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (    "Not all valleys can be crossed. Some remain fractured forever.") Tj ET
BT /F1 7.0 Tf 48.0 24.0 Td (Page 297 of 297) Tj ET
Q
